        <mxCell id="v21" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Module 9 changes a lifecycle state only through ILifecycleCommands.apply_decision() (one writer of lifecycle events, A8); the allowed decision kinds depend on the case type and hold reason (ADR-0003).&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; The evidence trail is derived from the event log, never stored separately (UC-D6).&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; ICaseIntake is realised inside the same database transaction as the hold or dispute event in iteration 1 (AR-3).&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; The scenario suite tests the engine only through IAssess; the held-out attack generator (iteration 3) is a separate package.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Relationship ends as in the Student 1 class diagram." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#F4F6F8;strokeColor=#8C99A6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="390" y="1025" width="700" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
